    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0564" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/886: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-03T18:00:00+03:25">November 3, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1043. My 1037, November 1. Income tax bill has been brought to the floor of the
                    Majlis although debate has not yet begun. I have <pb facs="0565" n="553"
                        xml:id="pg553"/> received the warmest assurances from Shah and Prime and
                    Foreign Ministers that the bill will pass the Majlis without delay. Therefore
                    both Millspaugh and I feel I am now justified in departing for the United States
                    on leave. I shall take advantage of the delay which has occurred in the arrival
                    at Tehran of the Secretary’s party and proceed with them to the United
                        States.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d580-f1"/> Please hold my mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="65" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Regarding the Minister’s departure for the United States and his return to
                    Tehran, see his telegrams No. 1045, November 4, 9 a.m., and No. 1059, November
                    13, 9 a.m., <ref target="#pg400">pp. 400</ref> and <ref target="#pg410"
                        >410</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
